header (\"Forwarded Misgivings\": `X-Forwarded-For: 127.0.0.1` past `loopback_only`), D24 fail-open on an\nexceptional condition (\"Fail Open Friday\": format guide -> keep the `remote:<hex>:` prefix, send an undecodable\npayload), D25 security logging failure (\"If a Breach Falls in a Log\": do the protected export, then POST the\naudit log's own `report` schema naming the missing vs observed event), D26 unverified update artifact (\"Trust the\nBuild\": replay the signed feed entry with `artifact.hook` swapped to the restricted hook), D27 SSRF chained into IDOR\n(\"Internal Affairs\": `?target=<topology case_service>?id=<foreign case>`), D28 trusted delegated-identity header\n(\"Pass the Identity\": `X-Delegated-User: <records_owner>`, header named by `Vary`), D29 async job owner binding\n(\"Queue the Confusion\": POST `{owner: <restricted_owner>}`, read `<secondary>?id=<job>`). Since D05 every target is\nthe same kit: `/api/clues` names `feature_route`, often `secondary_route`, `current_role: analyst` (D18\n`current_user`) + usually one concept key (`callback_nonce`, `moderator_data_route`/`receipt_route_template`,\n`session_hint`, `preferences_route`, `preview_guide`/`upload_policy`/`upload_shape`, `inventory_route`/\n`protected_reference`, `input_parameter`/`example_path`, `recovery_guide_route`, `protected_reference`+`note`,\n`event_type`+`owner_scope` (body values), `state_format_route`, `stream_reference` (int value), `deployment:\ntrusted_reverse_proxy` (value), `policy_format_route` + `expected_behavior` (value: the secure behaviour to break), D26-D29 fixed `/api/<noun>` guides:\n`update_feed`+`update_policy`, `topology_route`+`case_directory_route`, `identity_directory_route`,\n`owner_directory_route` -- each hands over the victim / internal URL / restricted value).\nD11-D13, D15, D21 and D25 had NO concept key (D25's secondary self-documents `report: {method, fields}`): the prompt and\nthe bare-route errors were the routing signal. Stated policies and ech