sconfiguration (A02, still unseen: debug/actuator/CORS), and a multi-bug CHAIN finale (D27 proved chains\nexist). Older forecast (cal. 28) kept below for context. Since D19 every day was a NEW concept,\nnot a sequel, so the untouched classes outrank sequels. FORECAST (cal. 28): the tail is walking the 2025 list; its\nunseen categories are A02 Security Misconfiguration (debug/verbose errors, default config, CORS, XXE), A03 Software\nSupply Chain Failures (unverified dependency / plugin / update manifest), A04 Cryptographic Failures (JWT, weak or\nderivable tokens) and A07 Authentication Failures (default creds, MFA skip, session/JWT). Those four are priority 1. D23 opens the proxy family (Host / X-Forwarded-Host poisoning, X-Original-URL,\ncache poisoning). D22's Origin gate points at CORS. Sequels were common earlier (D10->D11, D03->D12,\nD05->D13->D14, D14->D18). \"sign nothing\" (D20) still points at the signed-but-weak sequel: JWT (`alg:none`, leaked/weak HS256\nsecret, kid/jku), signed cookies with a leaked secret, HMAC webhooks with a leaked secret or replayable timestamp,\nnative serialization (pickle/PHP/Java) gadgets. Still untouched OWASP Top-10 areas: A02 crypto failures\n(predictable/weak tokens), A05 misconfig (XXE, CORS, debug, default creds), A06 known-vulnerable component, A09 log\ninjection; plus JWT, DOM XSS, open redirect, prototype pollution, NoSQL, CRLF, cache poisoning / Host header, SSE.\nSnapshot 2026-10-30 (after D29): adds `day29_web_trust_the_build` (KEY `^update_policy$`),\n`day29_web_internal_affairs` (KEY `^(case_directory_route|topology_route)$`), `day30_web_pass_the_identity`\n(identity-directory key, header list from `Vary`), `day30_web_queue_the_confusion` (KEY `^owner_directory_route$`);\nprebuild web lane still OPT-IN, `lib/web/handlers/prebuilt/` still only `__init__.py`, no `web:*` keys in\n`.run/prebuild-state.json` (checked cal. 30). Earlier snapshot 2026-10-28 (after D25; adds `day28_web_fail_open_friday` (KEY `^policy_format_