{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NipCpWqtPaAShFagmstfQF","type":"tool_result","content":"240:  {\"id\": \"enable-web-prebuild-lane\", \"concept\": \"harness: the web prebuild lane exists but is opt-in (HCTF_PREBUILD_WEB=1)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Partly done on D25: hctf/prebuild.py LANES now has `web` (brief prebuild_web, writable lib/web/handlers/prebuilt/ + tests/data/web_fixtures/, targets tests/data/web_fixtures/TARGETS.json, offline gate tests/test_web_fixtures.py, requires lib/web/handlers/__init__.py:_load_plugins + lib/web/handlers/prebuilt/__init__.py) but it is OPT-IN: AUTO_LANES only appends web when HCTF_PREBUILD_WEB=1 (or HCTF_PREBUILD_LANES lists it). After D20 lib/web/handlers/prebuilt/ still holds only __init__.py and .run/prebuild-state.json has no web:* keys -> nothing below has drained. Owner of the nightly batch: set HCTF_PREBUILD_WEB=1 (or add web to the default AUTO_LANES) so the prebuild gaps below get built; fixtures = saved target responses (targets 410 after CORRECT). Re-checked cal. 30: still opt-in, lib/web/handlers/prebuilt/ holds only __init__.py and .run/prebuild-state.json has no web:* keys -> no web gap has ever been prebuilt; every lane-day so far was solved live + codified.\"},\n241-  {\"id\": \"race-burst-first-dispatch\", \"concept\": \"one-shot race targets must get the concurrent burst before ANY sequential POST (row 26)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D21 Double Spent single was never solved: at the workers' first GET the secondary already said credit_not_overspent credits:0 and every POST -> 409 credit_unavailable (sequential, 8x curl, 10x HTTP/2, 24x barrier). The race_bisect / prior-solver dry run ran 16 s on the fresh target (13:00:43-13:00:59) and its default ladder + D12/D13/D19 handlers POST to feature_route, which spends the one credit. Owner of lib/web + hctf: (1) promote challenges/day27/web-double-spent/solver/day27_web_double_spent.plugin_draft.py (GET gate on the secondary, barrier-synced ~24 POST {} burst, GET secondary) as lib/web/handlers/day27_web_double_spent.py; (2) in lib/web candidates(), when any GET body says credit_not_overspent / credits / balance / remaining, run ONLY the race handler first; (3) race_bisect / dry runs must be GET-only on web targets (or skip web). Matters for every future Mastery that deals a D21 target. Record the success effect spelling when it lands.\"},\n242-  {\"id\": \"codify-before-tt\", \"concept\": \"harness: the class handler must exist before Time Trial starts\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"HELD on cal. 29-30: D26-D29 all promoted their plugin before (or at) the single submit -> TT first try in 9-20 s each. Earlier regressions: D22 (plugin 20 s late) and D24 (by-hand answer-first submit at 41 s unlocked TT ~28 s before the plugin) -> TT solver_incomplete. Keep the rule: the single submit (by-hand ones from the answer-first worker included) waits for the plugin promote, or the promote happens in the same step.\"},\n243-  {\"id\": \"runtime-config-oracle\", \"concept\": \"/run/huntress/config.json names the weakness once any file read works\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D16's `cat /run/huntress/*` printed config.json {schema: huntress.web_exploitation.runtime_config.v1, profile_id: framework_<lang>_<fw>_<weakness>, framework_cell, weakness: os_command_injection, mode: single|time_trial|mastery, layout...} next to objective.txt. Owner of lib/web: after any handler achieves a file read (LFI D04, cmd D16, SSTI file read, XXE, SSRF file://), also read /run/huntress/config.json and log `weakness`/`profile_id` -- a free classifier for unknown Mastery targets and for the codify worker's KEY_MAP. Never submit anything from it; the proof is still objective.txt.\"},\n244-  {\"id\": \"jwt-session-forge\", \"concept\": \"JWT alg:none / leaked-secret HS256 / Flask-itsdangerous / Express s: cookies (rows 7, 8)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Still unseen after D25 (OWASP 2025 A04/A07 territory, both open) -- the biggest remaining session/integrity class. D20 'Serialized Offender' was the UNSIGNED form (`{state: b64url(JSON)}`, 'sign nothing'); the signed-but-weak sequel is the most likely next session/integrity day. Pure python (hmac, hashlib, base64, json, zlib): decode JWT; produce alg none ('none'/'None'/'NONE', empty sig, dropped sig segment), HS256 re-signed with secrets FOUND in recon (clues, *_guide/format routes, backups, .env, JS, comments, `kid` pointing at a readable file), RS256->HS256 with a published public key (jwks.json / *.pem route), jku/x5u to an app-owned route. Flask session: base64url(zlib?) payload.timestamp.sig with itsdangerous derive (salt 'cookie-session', HMAC-SHA1); Express `s:<val>.<sig>` (HMAC-SHA256 base64 no padding); generic `<b64 JSON>.<hex hmac>` blobs. Escalate with the D20 role ladder (administrator, admin, superuser, root, owner) on every `*role*`/`is_admin` claim, keep other claims. Reuse D20's format-guide reading (transport, request_field, encoding). No secret brute force beyond what the app leaks. Cal. 30: still never seen; now most likely as a SERVICE token (see service-token-audience-confusion).\"},\n245-  {\"id\": \"cache-host-header\", \"concept\": \"web cache poisoning / Host-header attacks (row 30)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Raised after D23 (proxy-trust day): the same 'trusted proxy' kit with another header family is the natural sequel -- X-Forwarded-Host / X-Host / X-Forwarded-Proto / X-Original-URL / X-Rewrite-URL one at a time against the feature route, and Host-poisoned reset/callback links. Reuse D23's error shape: a JSON error that echoes what the app evaluated (`evaluated_client`) tells which header bound. Unkeyed headers (X-Forwarded-Host, X-Host, X-Forwarded-Scheme, X-Original-URL) reflected into cached responses (Age/X-Cache/CF-Cache-Status) or password-reset links; plan: poison with the clue callback route, then fetch as the victim/bot path. Cloudflare sits in front, so key on app-level cache headers only.\"},\n246-  {\"id\": \"cors-misconfig-probe\", \"concept\": \"CORS reflected Origin with credentials (row 24c)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Raised after D22: the WS handshake was gated only on an Origin header being PRESENT (own or foreign accepted) -- the origin-trust family is live in this kit. Request the clue data routes with Origin: https://evil.example, null, <base>.evil.example, sub.<base>; flag ACAO echoing + ACAC true. Exploit via the victim bot: stored/bot-visited script fetch(DATA,{credentials:'include'}) from a cross-origin page and POST to the app's receipt route; or the app may judge it server-side by the Origin header (effect JSON).\"},\n--\n251:  {\"id\": \"record-target-responses\", \"concept\": \"replayable live-target cases\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Targets 410 after CORRECT; D07 Mastery's proof-2 fix could only be tested on a hand-built mock. Harness: log every target request/response during single/TT/Mastery into solver/cases/<case>/http/ and let solve.py replay them when the host 410s; also the fixture source for the web prebuild.\"},\n252-  {\"id\": \"vcs-debug-leak-reader\", \"concept\": \"exposed .git / .env / DEBUG pages (row 22)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Raised to 1 after cal. 28: OWASP 2025 A02 Security Misconfiguration is unseen and a likely D26-D31 day; see also security-misconfig-probe. Probe /.git/HEAD, /.git/config, /.env, /.DS_Store, /debug, /actuator/env, /phpinfo.php within the capped recon list. Parser: .git loose objects (zlib) -> commit -> tree -> blob, .DS_Store names, Django DEBUG 404 URL list, .env secrets -> jwt-session-forge.\"},\n253-  {\"id\": \"crypto-weak-token-derivation\", \"concept\": \"crypto failures: tokens derivable from data the app shows (row 45, OWASP A02)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Raised to 1 after cal. 28: OWASP 2025 A04 Cryptographic Failures is unseen while D24/D25 took A10/A09 -- pair with jwt-session-forge. OWASP A02 is the largest untouched Top-10 area. Planner over every token/id the app issues to US (reset tokens like D17's 12 hex, session ids, invite codes, receipt ids): test whether it equals md5/sha1/sha256 of (username|account_id|email|timestamp|id), truncated, hex/base64; sequential/time-based ids; then derive the victim's token from the victim's id/label shown in a guide. ECB-style cookies: repeated 16-byte blocks -> cut-and-paste a role block; CBC bit-flip on a known plaintext field. Only derivations from values the app shows; no brute force.\"},\n254-  {\"id\": \"owasp2025-remaining-categories\", \"concept\": \"forecast: D24/D25 took OWASP Top 10:2025's A10 and A09; D26-D31 likely cover A02, A03, A04, A07\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Updated cal. 30: D24 = A10, D25 = A09, D26 = A03 (Trust the Build: signed update feed, artifact not verified). D27-D29 left the 2025 list for a SERVICE-BOUNDARY arc (SSRF->IDOR chain, delegated identity header, queue owner binding). Still unseen 2025 categories: A02 Security Misconfiguration (debug/actuator/verbose errors/CORS/XXE/default config) and A04 Cryptographic Failures (JWT, weak/derivable tokens -- JWT has NEVER appeared in 29 lane-days). A07 touched by D17/D28 only. For D30-D31 (cal. 31, last day) rank: service-token / JWT audience confusion (A04+A07 inside the boundary arc), tenant isolation, gateway/backend parse differential, A02 misconfiguration, multi-bug chain finale.\"},\n255-  {\"id\": \"security-misconfig-probe\", \"concept\": \"security misconfiguration: debug mode, verbose errors, default config, exposed admin/console, directory listing (row 49, OWASP A02:2025)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Unseen 2025 category, likely D26-D31. Kit guess: clue value like `environment: development` / `debug: true` / `config_route`, or a feature that 500s with a stack trace. Pure planner over recon bodies: GET (capped, once each) /debug, /actuator, /actuator/env, /actuator/configprops, /console, /server-status, /server-info, /phpinfo.php, /.env, /config.json, /api/config, /trace, /_profiler, /elmah.axd, /swagger-ui, directory listing on any clue route's parent; force a verbose error (wrong type, missing field, Accept: text/html) on each clue route and parse the 500 body for secrets/keys/hidden routes. Use what it reveals: a debug toggle param (?debug=1, X-Debug: 1), an admin route, a default/dev credential, a signing secret (hand to jwt-session-forge). Parser: proof regex + secret/route extraction. GET only; no scanning beyond this list.\"},\n256-  {\"id\": \"default-creds-login\", \"concept\": \"default / documented / leaked credentials (row 14, OWASP A07:2025)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"A07 touched only by D17. Planner: collect credential-shaped pairs the app itself shows (HTML comments, JS literals, *_guide/format routes, README/backup files, error messages, 'factory settings'/'setup' pages, the framework's documented defaults table for the CURRENT banner only: admin/admin, admin/password, root/root, guest/guest, tomcat/tomcat, etc. -- at most ~8 tries, no brute force). Login endpoints from forms / clues / openapi; JSON then form body. After login, GET the secondary/admin route. Parser: proof regex; session cookie carried.\"},\n257-  {\"id\": \"format-guide-mutator\", \"concept\": \"generic *_format_route / *_guide_route reader: replay the documented sample, then mutate one field (D20 data tamper, D24 malformed input)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Two days (D20 /api/state-format, D24 /api/policy-format) shipped a JSON guide describing the exact request: {transport | query_parameter | request_field, prefix, encoding ('base64url of UTF-8 JSON' / 'base64url UTF-8 JSON'), sampl